hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"361","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad and Ahmad bin Mansour Al-Ramadi told us, they said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said. H Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Jawhari, Abu Asim, told us on the authority of Ibn Jurayj. H Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Tasnim told us, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: When the Muslims came to Medina, they would gather to pray, but no one would call for it. One day they talked about that, and some of them said: They made a bell like the bell of the Christians, and some of them said: Rather, a horn like the horn of the Jews. Omar said: Will you not send a man to call to prayer? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Get up, O Bilal, and call for prayer.”"
"362","Bundar narrated to us, narrated to us Abu Bakr, meaning the Hanafi, narrated to us Abdullah bin Nafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Bilal used to say at the beginning He gave permission: “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He is alive to prayer.” Omar said to him: “Say after it: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,” so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Say as Omar commanded you.”"
